WEBVTT

00:02.574 --> 00:05.270
Hey, Charlie, would you see who that is?

00:12.384 --> 00:14.375
It's Death.

00:14.553 --> 00:16.111
Hi, Mom.

00:18.590 --> 00:20.888
Your gardener left this in the driveway.

00:21.393 --> 00:24.829
That was no gardener,
it was a girl with a grudge.

00:28.500 --> 00:32.061
- So how was your friend's funeral?
- Oh, terribly disappointing.

00:32.504 --> 00:37.237
Yeah, in my experience, nothing kills a party
like a dead broad in a box.

00:38.310 --> 00:39.971
Don't be glib, Charlie.

00:40.145 --> 00:42.170
- Hello, Alan.
Oh, hey, Mom.

00:42.347 --> 00:43.814
Wow, you look nice.

00:43.982 --> 00:46.109
Yes, mourning becomes me, doesn't it?

00:46.285 --> 00:48.845
If only more of my friends would die.

00:49.521 --> 00:51.785
I'm sure the feeling's mutual.

00:52.758 --> 00:55.420
Charlie, as long as you're over there,
make Mommy a drink.

00:55.594 --> 00:57.619
It's been a very depressing afternoon.

00:57.796 --> 00:59.821
Thanks for spreading it around.

00:59.998 --> 01:02.967
Can you believe two of Cynthia's
three children...

01:03.135 --> 01:06.070
...didn't even bother showing up
at her funeral?

01:06.238 --> 01:09.036
And the one who did was drunk
and cracking tasteless jokes...

01:09.208 --> 01:11.768
...about his mother
all throughout the service.

01:12.277 --> 01:15.110
You didn't happen to jot any of them down,
did you?

01:17.116 --> 01:19.107
And it wasrt just the children.

01:19.284 --> 01:23.778
The crowd was very sparse
and there was virtually no mourning.

01:23.956 --> 01:26.481
That's understandable.
You said no one liked this woman.

01:26.658 --> 01:29.821
Oh, she was a hateful shrew, but still...

01:30.596 --> 01:33.429
Fortunately, I was able to draw
on my theater background...

01:33.599 --> 01:35.965
...and work up a good cry.

01:36.135 --> 01:37.796
Sense memory.

01:37.970 --> 01:41.997
&lt;i>I remember the time I wasrt cast
as Blanche DuBois in Streetcar.&lt;/i>

01:42.875 --> 01:45.002
You're a good friend, Mom.

01:45.477 --> 01:48.844
I know. I'm just glad
that when my time comes...

01:49.014 --> 01:51.847
...I won't have
such a humiliating sendoff.

01:54.920 --> 01:56.046
Right?

01:56.221 --> 01:59.019
- Oh, yeah, yeah, sure. Yeah.
- Yeah, of course. Sendoff. Yes.

01:59.191 --> 02:01.056
Well, I'm gonna go freshen up.

02:01.226 --> 02:03.888
Even fake tears can ruin one's mascara.

02:04.062 --> 02:08.021
Whoever did Cynthia's makeup
should be shot and buried beside her.

02:08.200 --> 02:10.828
She looked like a varnished clown.

02:11.637 --> 02:14.128
You'll go to Mom's funeral, won't you?

02:14.673 --> 02:15.867
Of course.

02:16.041 --> 02:19.602
As the eldest son,
it's my obligation to pound in the stake.

02:21.280 --> 02:23.271
Typical. Nothing for Alan to do.

02:23.448 --> 02:28.385
Okay, you can cut off her head
and hold it up for the villagers.

02:36.728 --> 02:37.888
What are you doing?

02:38.063 --> 02:40.395
Leaving before Mom gets out
of the bathroom.

02:41.233 --> 02:44.999
- I thought we were taking her to dinner.
- I can't listen to her anymore.

02:45.170 --> 02:49.300
It blows my mind that she can go on and on
about her toxic friend's sad little funeral...

02:49.474 --> 02:51.999
...when we both know she gonna end up
the same way.

02:52.177 --> 02:55.169
I don't disagree, but there's an option
to running away from her.

02:55.347 --> 02:59.010
Yeah, but we'd get caught and
you'd sell me out for a reduced sentence.

02:59.184 --> 03:02.915
We could tell her the truth.
That she's just as toxic as her late friend...

03:03.088 --> 03:05.886
...and that that's the way
she's gonna be remembered.

03:08.260 --> 03:09.887
Are you on crack?

03:10.062 --> 03:13.793
Maybe if she realized how people see her,
she might make an effort to change.

03:13.966 --> 03:17.868
If she realized how people see her,
she'd just get new people.

03:18.036 --> 03:20.061
- Charlie, I...
- What are we gonna say, Alan?

03:20.239 --> 03:23.731
"You're a crazy she-bat and the only way
people will come to your funeral...

03:23.909 --> 03:27.868
...is if your delighted sons turn it into
a three-day beer bash with go-go dancers.

03:29.114 --> 03:31.378
Well, we wouldn't start there.

03:31.650 --> 03:34.118
All right, Cynthia's in the ground...

03:34.286 --> 03:36.345
...my face is on,
I look stunning in black...

03:36.521 --> 03:38.421
...let's go to dinner.

03:38.590 --> 03:40.217
Hey, just follow my lead.

03:42.761 --> 03:45.229
- Mom?
- Yes, dear.

03:49.835 --> 03:53.828
Alan thinks you're a crazy she-bat and
no one will mourn at your funeral either.

03:56.742 --> 04:00.178
We're telling you this
because we love you.

04:00.345 --> 04:01.778
I see.

04:01.947 --> 04:07.078
Look, Mom, you have to realize
that you're not that different from Cynthia.

04:07.519 --> 04:09.749
I most certainly am.

04:09.921 --> 04:13.687
Oh, come on, Mom. You speak ill
of everyone, even your closest friends.

04:13.859 --> 04:16.726
You manipulate people.
You're an unbelievable narcissist.

04:16.895 --> 04:20.092
- You're self-obsessed...
- That's a bit redundant, isn't it?

04:20.832 --> 04:23.960
You find fault with everything.

04:24.136 --> 04:27.799
And, frankly, I don't know anyone
who enjoys spending time with you...

04:27.973 --> 04:30.601
...let alone would cry at your funeral.

04:31.743 --> 04:33.608
That's one point of view.

04:38.183 --> 04:41.209
Charlie, I notice
you haven't said anything.

04:42.654 --> 04:45.953
Actually, "crazy she-bat" was mine.

04:48.327 --> 04:51.387
Again, Mom, we're only telling you this
because we care about you.

04:51.563 --> 04:53.690
Right, Charlie? We care about you.

04:53.865 --> 04:55.856
And it's not too late for you to change...

04:56.034 --> 04:59.333
...and become the kind of person
that people would dearly miss.

04:59.504 --> 05:01.267
When you're dead.

05:03.675 --> 05:07.042
- You've given me a lot to think about.
- Yes, and while you're thinking...

05:07.212 --> 05:09.680
...remember the spirit
in which it was intended.

05:10.482 --> 05:12.643
Oh, I won't forget that.

05:14.720 --> 05:15.744
Good, good.

05:15.921 --> 05:18.481
Listen, I think I'm gonna beg off dinner
tonight.

05:18.657 --> 05:21.182
Good, good. Aw.

05:24.296 --> 05:25.320
Goodbye, boys.

05:25.897 --> 05:27.888
Bye-bye.
- Goodbye.

05:33.572 --> 05:35.233
- Okay.
- Okay?

05:36.708 --> 05:38.938
What's okay?
What do you see that's okay?

05:39.411 --> 05:41.276
Well, we got out of dinner.

05:41.446 --> 05:42.913
Yes, but at what cost?

05:43.482 --> 05:47.851
Sure, her feelings are hurt right now,
but that'll pass in time...

05:48.019 --> 05:51.853
...and then she'll see this as an opportunity
to grow and change.

05:52.023 --> 05:53.718
Do you actually believe that?

05:54.993 --> 05:57.188
I have to, Charlie.

05:58.330 --> 06:00.230
I have to.

06:04.336 --> 06:06.304
Yo, mad props on the sandwich, Dad.

06:06.471 --> 06:09.099
This PB and J is off the hook.

06:10.275 --> 06:13.711
&lt;i>- Excuse me?
- He's been watching MTV Cribs.&lt;/i>

06:15.881 --> 06:17.371
The kid's a sponge.

06:17.549 --> 06:19.915
For shizzle, my dizzle.

06:20.085 --> 06:22.747
Hey, MC Skid Mark.

06:23.822 --> 06:26.791
Here's something else
you left in your pants.

06:28.093 --> 06:30.891
- Oh, right. I was supposed to mail this.
- What is it?

06:31.062 --> 06:34.190
It's a birthday card Mom gave me
to send to Grandma.

06:34.366 --> 06:36.960
Oh, God. Today's Mom's birthday.

06:37.135 --> 06:39.296
You forgot Mom's birthday?

06:39.938 --> 06:40.962
Did you remember it?

06:41.139 --> 06:44.575
Hey, hey, no one expects me
to remember anything.

06:44.743 --> 06:46.938
- Whers the last time you talked?
- I don't know.

06:47.112 --> 06:49.808
When we told her
she's horrible and nobody likes her.

06:49.981 --> 06:52.108
Oh, yeah. That was a fun day.

06:53.018 --> 06:56.954
- Guess I could save this for next year.
- No, no, no. You'll give it to her in person.

06:57.122 --> 06:59.420
We'll go buy her a present,
then bring it to her.

06:59.591 --> 07:01.786
Gee, Alan, she hasn't talked to us
in weeks.

07:01.960 --> 07:04.793
Don't you think showing up with a gift
might jeopardize that?

07:04.963 --> 07:07.090
If we don't,
we'll never hear the end of it.

07:07.265 --> 07:08.892
True dat.

07:09.835 --> 07:12.395
You tell them, Poop Dogg.

07:14.039 --> 07:17.133
Yo, check out the bling.

07:18.009 --> 07:19.636
Jake, I'm not gonna tell you again.

07:19.811 --> 07:22.939
You're a pasty white kid.
Start acting like one.

07:23.114 --> 07:24.445
Fine.

07:24.616 --> 07:25.708
Oh, this is cool.

07:28.920 --> 07:30.285
It does say, "Mom. "

07:31.056 --> 07:33.957
Charlie, be serious.
Jake, if you wanna help, find something...

07:34.125 --> 07:36.616
...that's appropriate for your grandma.
- Like what?

07:37.028 --> 07:40.794
See if they got a grizzly bear
ripping apart a salmon.

07:43.902 --> 07:46.200
Hi there. May I help you find something?

07:46.371 --> 07:49.306
Oh, yeah. We're looking for a birthday gift
for our mother.

07:49.474 --> 07:51.135
Oh, how sweet. Whers her birthday?

07:51.776 --> 07:53.334
Today.

07:53.512 --> 07:55.036
He forgot.

07:55.213 --> 07:58.205
Well, tell me something about her.
What does she like?

07:58.383 --> 07:59.816
Hurting people.

08:00.519 --> 08:01.543
Charlie...

08:01.720 --> 08:05.588
It's a little hard to answer that
because we have a strained relationship.

08:05.757 --> 08:09.693
Oh, so you'd like to find a gift
that would help bring you closer together?

08:10.228 --> 08:12.423
- No, no. No, no.
- Oh, no. No.

08:13.498 --> 08:15.728
This is just your standard
family obligation...

08:15.901 --> 08:19.200
...here it is, happy birthday,
stay-off-our-backs kind of thing.

08:19.671 --> 08:21.662
But with a pretty bow.

08:22.474 --> 08:25.170
I see. And what is your price range?

08:26.645 --> 08:28.909
Enough that she can't complain,
but not so much...

08:29.080 --> 08:31.844
...that it's won'th her while to return it.
- Exactly.

08:32.784 --> 08:36.049
Have you considered a nice perfume?

08:36.221 --> 08:37.449
Do you know her scent?

08:37.622 --> 08:38.919
- Oh, actually I don't.
- I do.

08:39.090 --> 08:40.387
- You do?
- Yep.

08:40.559 --> 08:42.390
Do you carry Chanel N° 666?

08:44.429 --> 08:48.661
You know, I think I'm going to let
the two of you just browse a bit more...

08:48.833 --> 08:51.893
...and I'll be back, maybe.

08:52.470 --> 08:54.301
Great news.

08:54.472 --> 08:56.463
It's on sale.

08:59.744 --> 09:01.939
Now, remember,
this was not a last-minute thing.

09:02.113 --> 09:04.047
Our plan all along was to surprise her.

09:04.215 --> 09:06.445
I know how to lie, Dad.

09:07.085 --> 09:08.985
We're not lying. We're being considerate.

09:09.154 --> 09:10.280
By lying.

09:13.291 --> 09:14.724
Happy birthday.

09:14.893 --> 09:17.384
Oh, what a surprise.

09:17.562 --> 09:19.655
That was the plan all along.

09:20.999 --> 09:22.660
I don't know what to say.

09:22.834 --> 09:25.064
After the last time we spoke,
I assumed that...

09:25.236 --> 09:26.260
Come on, Mom.

09:26.438 --> 09:30.499
No matter what, you're still our mother.
Right, Charlie? You're still our mother.

09:31.543 --> 09:33.067
Give her her present, Jake.

09:33.244 --> 09:34.973
- Happy birthday.
- Thank you.

09:35.146 --> 09:37.444
- Oh, it's heavy.
- It's just a bowl.

09:37.616 --> 09:39.743
I wanted to get you a bear eating a fish.

09:41.086 --> 09:44.249
But we got her a nice crystal bowl
instead.

09:45.490 --> 09:48.789
- So can we come in?
- Actually, I'm having a little party.

09:49.294 --> 09:51.262
- A party?
- And you didn't invite us?

09:51.630 --> 09:54.394
Charles, if someone's not going to mourn
at my funeral...

09:54.566 --> 09:57.933
...I certainly don't want them
at my birthday party.

09:58.303 --> 10:00.168
Well, then who's here?

10:01.139 --> 10:04.768
People who love me. People who care
about me and accept me for who I am.

10:06.111 --> 10:07.544
Oh, I gotta see this.

10:08.647 --> 10:10.478
Please come in.

10:12.851 --> 10:14.182
Oh, hello.

10:15.387 --> 10:16.445
Hi.

10:16.621 --> 10:22.491
Charlie, Alan, Jake, I'd like you to meet
Roger and Philip and their son, Changpu.

10:22.661 --> 10:24.458
These are my sons and grandson.

10:24.629 --> 10:26.153
- Oh, hi.
- Nice to meet you.

10:26.331 --> 10:28.595
Your mom is such an incredible woman.

10:28.767 --> 10:32.430
- She's like the loving mother I never had.
- She's fabulous.

10:32.604 --> 10:34.196
We're one big, happy family.

10:38.143 --> 10:41.977
Son of a bitch. She got new people.

10:46.918 --> 10:48.180
Who are these guys?

10:48.653 --> 10:50.143
You're surprised I have friends?

10:50.321 --> 10:52.516
You're surprised that I'm surprised?

10:52.691 --> 10:55.353
Roger works in my real-estate office,
Philip does my hair.

10:55.527 --> 10:58.325
And I introduced them.
They make a lovely couple, don't they?

10:58.863 --> 10:59.921
Yeah, I guess.

11:00.098 --> 11:01.429
And they adopted...

11:02.233 --> 11:03.257
...Chung King?

11:04.669 --> 11:07.263
Changpu. Yes, from China.

11:07.439 --> 11:11.136
Of course, I had to help them a bit,
greasing the bureaucratic wheels.

11:11.309 --> 11:13.573
- You bribed someone?
- Oh, don't be ridiculous.

11:13.745 --> 11:15.440
I merely slept with a commie.

11:17.482 --> 11:20.451
- Is this goose liver?
- It's quail pâté with endive.

11:20.618 --> 11:23.143
- Philip's special recipe.
- Oh, you gotta give it to me.

11:23.321 --> 11:25.949
Well, I'll trade you.
My recipe for your mother.

11:26.124 --> 11:27.955
Done.

11:28.126 --> 11:31.789
You are so lucky.
My mother is a bitch on wheels.

11:31.963 --> 11:35.160
- Your mother? What about my mother?
- Fine, your mother's a bitch too.

11:35.333 --> 11:37.198
Thank you.

11:38.036 --> 11:41.028
So do you have a PlayStation or an Xbox?

11:41.206 --> 11:43.003
I have a cello.

11:43.408 --> 11:47.708
- What do you play on that?
- Beethoven, Brahms, Bach, Shostakovich.

11:47.879 --> 11:49.744
So no "Grand Theft Auto"?

12:01.860 --> 12:03.919
Oh, this is a treat.

12:15.240 --> 12:18.801
My boys, my boys. Thank you.

12:18.977 --> 12:22.174
- Make a wish.
- Why? You're already here.

12:22.347 --> 12:23.837
My wish has come true.

12:27.652 --> 12:30.018
Who wishes for two gay guys
and a Chinese kid?

12:32.390 --> 12:36.588
Oh, and now, Evy,
we have a very special present for you.

12:37.529 --> 12:40.089
What do you think,
a bear eating a bear?

12:41.633 --> 12:44.101
Changpu is going to perform
a cello concerto.

12:44.269 --> 12:46.328
He wrote it himself in your honor.

12:46.504 --> 12:48.096
How marvelous.

12:52.210 --> 12:56.237
- Should I give her the card now?
- Forget about the card, Jake.

12:56.414 --> 13:00.214
Shh, shh, shh. Shampoo is gonna play.

13:10.128 --> 13:13.928
Don't feel bad.
I bet he can't burp the alphabet.

13:17.468 --> 13:21.302
Well, that was one of the most
bizarre evenings I've ever spent.

13:21.472 --> 13:24.407
- It was right up there.
- I thought it was fabulous.

13:27.979 --> 13:29.674
You know what's happened, don't you?

13:29.848 --> 13:32.646
- We've been replaced.
- Hey, fine with me.

13:33.017 --> 13:36.453
As long as she's got Siegfried and Roy,
we don't have to deal with her.

13:36.621 --> 13:39.784
It's fine with me too. I just can't believe
she conned these guys...

13:39.958 --> 13:43.416
...into thinking she's a good witch.
- Well, we know she's not.

13:43.595 --> 13:46.325
- You're damn right.
- You said it, sister.

13:47.365 --> 13:50.994
Hey, SpongeBob GayPants, take a break.

13:53.805 --> 13:57.070
You don't think
we might have been wrong about Mom.

13:57.709 --> 14:00.177
- What?
- I'm just saying that Roger and Philip...

14:00.345 --> 14:02.540
...obviously see something in her
that we don't.

14:02.714 --> 14:04.477
Who knows her better? Us or them?

14:04.649 --> 14:05.911
Oh, us. No question.

14:06.084 --> 14:08.177
But maybe there's a part of her
we're missing.

14:08.353 --> 14:10.821
Alan, there's a part of her she's missing.

14:11.022 --> 14:12.614
It's called her soul.

14:12.790 --> 14:14.553
Snap.

14:25.603 --> 14:27.002
Hey, Mom, how are you?

14:27.171 --> 14:29.639
Charlie, what a pleasant surprise.

14:29.807 --> 14:33.368
Oh, I was just calling to say happy birthday
again and thanks for last night.

14:33.544 --> 14:37.002
It was so nice to meet Philip and Roger...

14:37.181 --> 14:39.206
...and Shanghai.

14:39.384 --> 14:40.715
Changpu.

14:40.885 --> 14:45.117
&lt;i>- And thank you for the lovely crystal bowl.
- Oh, good, you like it?&lt;/i>

14:45.290 --> 14:47.087
Like it? Well, I love it.

14:47.258 --> 14:49.522
I'm admiring it right now.

14:50.528 --> 14:51.654
Great, great.

14:51.829 --> 14:54.263
&lt;i>- Listen, dear, I've really gotta go.
- No, wait, Mom.&lt;/i>

14:54.432 --> 14:57.868
I wanna clear the air about that stuff
that got said a couple of weeks ago.

14:58.036 --> 14:59.435
What's that?

14:59.604 --> 15:02.767
Well, I don't have any problems
with you being who you are.

15:02.941 --> 15:08.106
That whole thing about you needing
to change, well, that's Alars deal.

15:08.279 --> 15:10.372
&lt;i>- Oh, I knew that.
- Yeah.&lt;/i>

15:10.548 --> 15:12.607
The thing I love about
our relationship is...

15:12.784 --> 15:15.719
...that you don't try to change me,
I don't try to change you.

15:15.887 --> 15:19.448
We accept each other as, you know,
incapable of changing.

15:19.624 --> 15:20.989
That is very sweet.

15:21.159 --> 15:25.186
Okay, here you go.
Eggs Benedict, my own reci...

15:26.531 --> 15:29.523
- Anything else?
- No, no, I guess not.

15:29.901 --> 15:33.428
- Love you.
- You too. Bye-bye.

15:33.771 --> 15:37.036
- Who was that?
- Oh, nobody.

15:37.208 --> 15:40.609
You said there was something important
you wanted to talk to me about?

15:40.778 --> 15:43.770
Yeah, yeah. I was just thinking about...

15:43.948 --> 15:46.212
Mm. Mm.
Too much lemon juice in the sauce.

15:46.384 --> 15:47.578
Oh, gee, I'm sorry.

15:48.186 --> 15:49.915
You should ask Philip for his recipe.

15:51.155 --> 15:55.319
- I will.
- You might also ask him who cuts his hair.

15:55.727 --> 15:58.628
You don't have to be gay to look nice.

16:00.798 --> 16:02.493
I'll ask.

16:02.734 --> 16:05.567
Anyway, I just wanted to clear the air
about a few things.

16:06.037 --> 16:08.301
Really? Like what?

16:08.873 --> 16:14.402
Well, you know, that stuff that got said
a couple of weeks ago.

16:14.579 --> 16:17.013
I just want you to know...

16:17.181 --> 16:18.944
...it was Charlie's idea.

16:19.550 --> 16:21.074
Oh, I knew that.

16:21.953 --> 16:24.217
Yeah, I only went along because,
you know...

16:24.389 --> 16:26.357
...he's the older brother...

16:26.524 --> 16:27.991
...and he might have been drunk.

16:28.860 --> 16:31.693
Well, I'm just glad one of my sons
cares about me.

16:31.863 --> 16:34.127
I do. I love you, Mommy.

16:35.333 --> 16:36.425
Right back at you.

16:36.934 --> 16:39.903
Now skedaddle.
Philip and Roger will be here any minute.

16:40.071 --> 16:43.040
Oh. Okay.

16:44.308 --> 16:47.106
Oh, look, there they are.

16:47.945 --> 16:50.038
Philip, Roger and Changpu.

16:51.549 --> 16:54.450
No pictures of me or Jake.

16:55.086 --> 16:58.988
Sweetheart, I've been asking
for a decent picture for years.

16:59.157 --> 17:01.421
All I've ever gotten was a school photo
of Jake...

17:01.592 --> 17:03.856
...where he appeared to be sucking
on his shirt.

17:04.028 --> 17:07.657
Oh, yeah. They served spaghetti
on picture day.

17:08.032 --> 17:10.262
Oh, hey, you know
what we should do?

17:10.435 --> 17:13.199
We should get together
and take a nice family portrait.

17:13.371 --> 17:15.464
- That sounds lovely.
- Great. I'll set it up.

17:15.640 --> 17:18.734
- Terrific.
- Okay. Bye.

17:18.910 --> 17:20.537
Bye-bye.

17:22.346 --> 17:24.371
Did I tell you that I love you, Mommy?

17:25.083 --> 17:27.483
Yes, but I never tire of hearing it.

17:27.652 --> 17:31.383
Oh, well, in that case,
I love you, Mommy.

17:36.094 --> 17:39.621
I really should have stopped drinking
during pregnancy.

17:55.546 --> 17:58.242
- Hello?
- Hello.

18:04.522 --> 18:06.956
- Hey, Alan?
- Yeah?

18:07.492 --> 18:10.928
I couldn't help noticing
there's a photographer in the living room.

18:11.095 --> 18:14.030
Oh, yeah, we're taking a family picture.

18:14.665 --> 18:16.530
Family picture.

18:17.602 --> 18:21.538
Would it be rude of me to point out
the obvious flaw in your plan?

18:21.706 --> 18:24.231
- I didn't think you'd be interested.
- I'm not.

18:25.776 --> 18:29.268
So it's just you
and Little Lord Scratch 'r Sniff?

18:29.447 --> 18:33.281
Hey, if you don't sniff it,
you don't know what it is.

18:36.721 --> 18:39.781
Actually, it's a picture
of me, Jake and Mom.

18:41.125 --> 18:43.389
Mom? Mom who?

18:44.462 --> 18:47.625
She said she didn't have
any good pictures of us.

18:48.299 --> 18:51.029
Wait a minute,
when did you talk to Mom?

18:52.203 --> 18:53.830
She called me.

18:54.338 --> 18:57.000
You've been sucking up to her
behind my back, haven't you?

18:57.742 --> 19:02.611
Charlie, you have no idea
how insane that sounds.

19:03.247 --> 19:05.442
All I know is after everything
that's happened...

19:05.616 --> 19:08.278
...I would never talk to her
without talking to you first.

19:08.452 --> 19:11.853
- You wouldn't?
- What kind of person do you take me for?

19:12.023 --> 19:17.290
I'd rather cut off my arm than pick up
the phone and try to undermine my brother.

19:17.461 --> 19:19.156
Me too.

19:19.330 --> 19:21.321
That's why I'm...

19:21.599 --> 19:23.590
...taking a bullet here for the both of us.

19:25.570 --> 19:26.832
Well, thanks.

19:27.305 --> 19:29.296
You don't have to thank me.

19:29.574 --> 19:30.768
I'm your brother.

19:32.543 --> 19:34.272
Ooh. Mommy's here.

19:35.613 --> 19:37.843
Might as well get this over with.

19:38.082 --> 19:40.050
Wait a sec, hang on.

19:40.585 --> 19:41.779
Let me go change.

19:41.953 --> 19:44.319
- You actually wanna be in the picture?
No, no, no.

19:44.488 --> 19:45.716
Are you kidding?

19:45.890 --> 19:48.518
But it's not fair for you
to have to do it alone.

19:49.293 --> 19:51.955
Oh. Well, thanks.

19:52.129 --> 19:55.155
You don't have to thank me.
I'm your brother.

19:58.302 --> 20:00.133
- Hi, Mom.
- Hello, dear.

20:00.304 --> 20:02.636
- Mom, how are you? Good to see you.
- Hi, Charlie.

20:02.807 --> 20:05.833
Oh, what a marvelous house.

20:06.010 --> 20:08.911
- Adorable.
- Mom?

20:09.080 --> 20:12.311
You said you wanted a family portrait.
They're family.

20:14.652 --> 20:16.813
Okay, well, I'm going back to bed.

20:16.988 --> 20:18.683
Charlie, what about the picture?

20:18.856 --> 20:21.188
Put me down for a wallet size.

20:21.359 --> 20:23.520
I just love what you're wearing.

20:48.686 --> 20:49.778
- Like that?
- Yeah.

20:49.954 --> 20:52.718
But what was all that crap
in the beginning?

20:52.890 --> 20:55.188
Introduction of my own composition.

20:55.359 --> 20:57.793
No offense, but "Smoke on the Water"
doesn't begin...

20:57.962 --> 21:00.157
...with crap on the water.

21:01.332 --> 21:02.356
My apologies.

21:02.533 --> 21:06.970
Okay, let's take it from the top.
One, two, three, four.

21:15.279 --> 21:17.247
The play date was a good idea.

21:17.415 --> 21:20.145
Yeah, let's see
how Grandma likes her prodigy...

21:20.318 --> 21:23.879
...after he sponges up our sponge.
